      "id": "sol.amc-12a-2016-p2.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Since \\(100=10^2\\) and \\(1000=10^3,\\) the equation becomes \\[ 10^x\\cdot 10^{4x}=10^{15}, \\] so \\(10^{5x}=10^{15}.\\) Then \\(5x=15,\\) giving \\(x=3.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is C.",
      "hints": [
        "Write every base as a power of \\(10\\)",
        "The left side becomes \\(10^{5x}\\) and the right side \\(10^{15}\\)"
      ],
